  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed works have already been substantially completed, by reason of the existing alterations to the fabric of the first floor level living room, and its removal as common space. This renders the existing plans as submitted inaccurate, and places the development outside of the scope of S191 of the Town and Country Planning Act (as amended). ",
    "The change from 7 person HMO (sui generis) to 8 person HMO (sui generis)  would materially alter the character of the site’s usage, including a reduction in living conditions for future occupants, in addition to the loss of communal space, as well as the additional pressures on site amenities and potential disturbance generated to existing occupants,. Therefore the proposal will require a full assessment under planning permission. As there is no such extant permission, the development is considered unlawful"
  ],
